course: dictionary
lesson: 11626
title: Natural talent: aptitude
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An aptitude is a natural ability, a talent you seem to have from the start. It means you can learn something quickly or do it well. «Mia has an aptitude for music: she picked up the tune after hearing it just once.» The clue is quickly. Mia did not practise for weeks, so her talent came naturally.
explain: Look for the small words that go with aptitude. You say an aptitude for something, such as an aptitude for maths. You can also show aptitude, and schools may give an aptitude test. «The aptitude test showed that Sam had a real talent for drawing.» A test cannot make a talent, so it must measure one that is already there.
explain: Do not mix up aptitude with skill. Aptitude is the talent you start with. Skill is what you build by practising. «Ravi has the aptitude to play the piano, but he needs months of practice to play it well.» Good aptitude gives you a head start, and practice does the rest.
fact: Aptitude means a natural ability or talent to do something well or to learn it quickly.
fact: Aptitude is a noun: an aptitude, several aptitudes.
fact: You can say «an aptitude for» something, such as «an aptitude for languages».
fact: An aptitude test measures what a person might be good at.
fact: Aptitude is a natural talent, while skill is something you build through practice.
exercise: «Ella has an aptitude for languages.» What does aptitude mean? | A place to play | A rule you must always obey | A sad feeling | *A natural talent for something
exercise: «The school gave every child an aptitude test.» What is an aptitude test for? | To check the weather | To decide what is for lunch | To count the pupils in the hall | *To find out what a child could be good at
exercise: Which small word completes the phrase «an aptitude ___ maths»? | from | *for | with | at
test: «Zara learns new coding quickly, so she clearly has real aptitude.» What does aptitude mean here? | Bad luck | *A natural ability to learn quickly | Tiredness after a long day | A type of bicycle
test: Which phrase means having a natural talent for music? | Music lessons on Friday | Loud music at lunchtime | *An aptitude for music | A music case for the trumpet
exam: «Owen's aptitude test showed he could build things well.» Which word is closest in meaning to aptitude? | Delay | Holiday | *Talent | Mistake
